		"follow": {"say": "You set the chisel to the stone below the cut line. It goes in more easily than stone should. You cut: AND THEN I FOLLOW. Somewhere in the sky above the Crossing, something takes a breath it has been holding for nine winters, and for a moment the turning slows.", "who": "", "do": "qp:aurel_edicts:follow,qa:aurel_edicts", "next": ""},
		"leave": {"say": "You close the copy-book. The stone says what it says. You lay your hand flat against it, as a witness does, and nothing answers, and that is an answer.", "who": "", "do": "qp:aurel_edicts:leave,qa:aurel_edicts", "next": ""},
		"scratch": {"say": "You drag the chisel across the edict, line by line, until the stone is a smear. Dust comes away. It is very quiet. The sky overhead turns on, a little faster, as if it had been told it was not being watched.", "who": "", "do": "qp:aurel_edicts:scratch,qa:aurel_edicts", "next": ""},
