		"stair": {"say": "You tip the coal into the lamp and turn the glass to the mountain. The wick takes. All down the road behind you, post after post, the lamps swing a quarter-turn and lean the same way, toward the Stair. The long line of them holds, like an argument that has finally been made.", "who": "", "do": "qp:lamp_road:stair,qa:lamp_road", "next": ""},
		"home": {"say": "You tip the coal into the lamp and turn the glass toward Hearthward. The wick takes. All down the road behind you, post after post, the lamps swing a quarter-turn and face the village. The whole road becomes a long hand held out to whoever is on it.", "who": "", "do": "qp:lamp_road:home,qa:lamp_road", "next": ""},
		"gone": {"say_if": [["qp:lamp_road:stair", "The lamps lean toward the Stair."], ["qp:lamp_road:home", "The lamps face Hearthward."], ["", "The post stands at the Stair's foot, dark."]], "who": "", "next": ""},
	}},
	"story_roll": {"name": "The Tally Post", "start": [["qat:name_on_roll:5", "post"], ["", "gone"]], "nodes": {
		"post": {"say": "The Tally post has one line left, under ONE LATE PILGRIM, NO NAME. A nail hangs on a string beside it, for cutting. Seren Marsh's name is above, and the line below it is empty. You are the only other late pilgrim for a very long way. The wind has stopped.", "who": "", "choices": [
			{"text": "Cut your own name in the empty line. Enter yourself.", "to": "entered"},
			{"text": "Cut Seren Marsh's child's name, Ione, in the line, in her mother's hand.", "to": "mother"},
			{"text": "Leave the line blank.", "to": "blank"},
			{"text": "Not yet.", "to": ""},
		]},
		"entered": {"say": "You cut it with the nail, slowly: a name the Order never knew, from a face that has not had one in nine winters. The stone takes it. When you step back, the line reads, in your own letters, a name. The post is warm under your hand, the way a hand is warm.", "who": "", "do": "qp:name_on_roll:entered,qa:name_on_roll", "next": ""},
		"mother": {"say": "You cut IONE, in small, careful letters, in the line her mother left empty. The nail goes in without a sound. The post, which has been cold for nine winters, is a little warmer. Somewhere beyond the Fen a child's hand, long grown, closes.", "who": "", "do": "qp:name_on_roll:mother,qa:name_on_roll", "next": ""},
		"blank": {"say": "You lay the nail down on the string. The line stays empty, as the Abbot's book never would have left it. The wind comes back, a little, round the post's foot, and the whole Tally seems to settle, like a ledger that has not been balanced and does not mind.", "who": "", "do": "qp:name_on_roll:blank,qa:name_on_roll", "next": ""},
		"gone": {"say_if": [["qp:name_on_roll:entered", "The last line of the roll is cut with a name that is yours."], ["qp:name_on_roll:mother", "IONE, in small letters, under SEREN."], ["", "The last line of the Tally is blank."]], "who": "", "next": ""},
	}},
	"story_horn": {"name": "The Horn", "start": [["qat:horn_end:5", "horn"], ["", "gone"]], "nodes": {
		"horn": {"say": "The horn's mouth is as wide as a doorway and smooth as the inside of a shell, and the note comes out of it, steady and thin and tireless. At its foot, a stool. On the stool, nothing. Lowe's torn page is in your hand: the Hierarch's edict, set for one voice, with the last line cut away. You have heard it. You think you know where it goes.", "who": "", "choices": [
			{"text": "Sing the verse's last line: that is enough, now.", "to": "sung"},
			{"text": "Break the horn's lip with a hammer.", "to": "broke"},
			{"text": "Leave the note ringing.", "to": "left"},
			{"text": "Not yet.", "to": ""},
		]},
		"sung": {"say": "You sing it, badly, at the pitch the note gives you, four words in the Order's old cadence: that is enough, now. The note wavers, for the first time in nine winters, and holds a moment longer, and is only a note again. Somewhere high up the skull a small throat clears itself, as if for sleep.", "who": "", "do": "qp:horn_end:sung,qa:horn_end", "next": ""},
		"broke": {"say": "You swing the hammer at the horn's lip. The stone rings. A chip comes away as long as your forearm, and the note falters, cracks, and goes on a little thinner than before. It is not stopped. It is only wounded. Every cantor in the Lines will hear it.", "who": "", "do": "qp:horn_end:broke,qa:horn_end", "next": ""},
		"left": {"say": "You lay the torn page on the stool and go away from the horn. The note follows you as far as the gate: steady, bright, and nothing like a cry. It does not sound like a boy who needs to be rescued. It sounds like a boy who is keeping his word.", "who": "", "do": "qp:horn_end:left,qa:horn_end", "next": ""},
		"gone": {"say_if": [["qp:horn_end:sung", "The horn is quiet but for a faint breath."], ["qp:horn_end:broke", "The horn's lip is chipped, and the note is thin."], ["", "The horn rings on."]], "who": "", "next": ""},
	}},
	"story_wall": {"name": "The Cell Wall", "start": [["qat:vow_cell:4", "wall"], ["", "gone"]], "nodes": {
		"wall": {"say": "The niche at the wall's foot is dark. You can hear someone breathing in it: slow, tidy, exact. The loaf is warm in your hands. Tamsin has told you everything she knows. It was not much. The vow is cut round the niche in a ring, with no beginning and no end.", "who": "", "choices": [
			{"text": "Leave the loaf on the shelf, and go.", "to": "bread"},
			{"text": "Say her name through the wall.", "to": "name"},
